The attached image (Fig 3) illustrates the transient inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 at the injection site. Panel (a) shows the kinetics of various inflammatory cells, with neutrophils peaking early (6h-Day 1) and declining, while Mac-2+ macrophages, antigen-presenting cells, and Ly6C+ monocytes accumulate later (peaking around Day 2). Panel (b) presents confocal microscopy images demonstrating that Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 (red) is taken up intracellularly by MHCII+ cells, Ly6C+ monocytes, and Mac-2+ macrophages (green) over time, with negligible uptake by 1A8+ neutrophils, confirming its phagocytosis by recruited cells and a transient inflammatory profile.